GTKTest - riscos-gtk M1 tests

Checks the libraries riscos-gtk (GTK 3 for RISC OS) is built on.

glibtest: GLib - the main loop, threads, files (including an
asynchronous read on a worker thread), GObject signals, GVariant, GRegex,
iconv, UTF-8, key files, dates and printf.

rendertest: the drawing stack GTK uses for every widget - fontconfig
finding DejaVu Sans, pango laying out text (harfbuzz for kerning, fribidi
for right-to-left text), cairo and pixman drawing it with shapes and a
scaled pattern, and gdk-pixbuf writing and reading PNG and JPEG.

Double-click !GTKTest. A task window shows lines "ok N - ..." and each
test ends with "N checks, F failed". The same output is saved in the
Result file inside the application, and the picture the render test
drew in rendertest (a PNG). Send back Result (and rendertest if it
looks wrong), with a note of anything else that happened.

The first run builds a font cache in the scrap directory, so it is
slower; the output says how long the first text took.

Needs SharedUnixLibrary 1.16+, ARMEABISupport and Iconv (PackMan).
PThreadTicker 0.03 is included (from riscos-unixlib 5.0.3.1).

